sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device as Medical Device
    participant TLS as Gateway TLS Layer
    participant EST as EstController
    participant Orch as EnrollmentOrchestrator
    participant PKCS as PkcsService
    participant DB as Gateway Database
    participant Factory as CaConnectorFactory
    participant CA as Active CA Backend
    participant Notify as NotificationDispatcher

    Device->>Device: Load existing PFX certificate and private key
    Device->>Device: Generate new key pair
    Device->>Device: Build renewal CSR with same subject CN
    Device->>TLS: Open HTTPS connection with existing client certificate
    TLS-->>EST: ClientCertificate available on request
    Device->>EST: POST /.well-known/est/simplereenroll with CSR

    EST->>DB: Resolve enabled EST profile by host and path
    DB-->>EST: EST profile id
    EST->>EST: Require client certificate
    EST->>EST: Check client cert validity window
    opt Profile validates client cert chain
        EST->>EST: Build chain and require configured trusted CA thumbprint
    end
    EST->>PKCS: Decode EST request body
    PKCS-->>EST: CSR bytes
    EST->>Orch: ReenrollAsync(profileId, csr, existingCert, clientIp)

    Orch->>Orch: Check existing cert NotBefore and NotAfter
    Orch->>DB: Load EST profile
    DB-->>Orch: Enabled profile
    Orch->>DB: Find stored certificate by thumbprint or serial
    DB-->>Orch: Existing certificate record
    Orch->>Orch: Require same EST profile and CertificateStatus.Valid
    Orch->>DB: Resolve device by certificate DeviceRecordId or subject CN
    DB-->>Orch: Device record
    Orch->>Orch: Require device Status = Active and RemovedAt is null
    Orch->>PKCS: ParsePkcs10(csr)
    PKCS-->>Orch: Parsed CSR
    Orch->>Orch: Require CSR CN matches existing device CN

    alt Re-enrollment is not allowed
        Orch->>Notify: NotifyEnrollmentRejectedAsync
        Notify-->>Orch: Notification attempted if enabled
        Orch-->>EST: Failed(reason, 403)
        EST-->>Device: 403 JSON error
    else Re-enrollment is allowed
        Orch->>DB: Load active CA backend
        DB-->>Orch: Active enabled backend
        Orch->>PKCS: Validate CSR signature
        PKCS-->>Orch: Valid
        Orch->>DB: Insert pending EnrollmentEvent
        Orch->>Factory: CreateConnector(active backend)
        Factory-->>Orch: ICaConnector
        Orch->>CA: IssueCertificateAsync(csr, profile)
        CA-->>Orch: Renewed certificate and chain
        Orch->>DB: Store new Certificate metadata
        Orch->>DB: Update Device.LastCertificateId
        Orch->>DB: Mark EnrollmentEvent Issued
        Orch->>PKCS: Encode renewed chain as PKCS#7 EST response
        PKCS-->>Orch: Base64 response body
        Orch-->>EST: Successful(PKCS#7 response)
        EST-->>Device: 200 application/pkcs7-mime
        Device->>Device: Install renewed certificate with new private key
    end
